2042 (Dan): vdist() now measures campus (U['school_coords']) to bowl host city (U['city_coords']) instead of state label to state label. Applies to every neutral round (QF, SF) from 2042 on; the championship site is fixed and unaffected. Backup: committee.py.pre_school_dist. 2042 QF assignment under the new rule: Dietsche-Hoganelle 501, Tasson-Barhold Redwood, Eona-Fiota Bay Lumber, Ranroman State-Pistolheart Copper.
2042 (Dan): rotation_venue now takes the opponent; the higher seed skips any bowl located in the opponent's own state (de facto home game), falling back to plain nearest only if every free bowl is one. playoff._neutral_round passes the lower seed. Backups: committee.py.pre_oppo_home, playoff.py.bak_oppo. 2042 QF sites: Dietsche-Hoganelle 501 (Stamford); Tasson-Barhold Redwood (Kirkwood); Eona-Fiota Bay Copper (Billiataho); Ranroman State-Pistolheart Lumber (Port Logan).
2042 (Dan): from 2043 (season 18) the semifinal bowls are always one of three fixed pairs: Copper-Steam, Lumber-Star, Redwood-501, cycling every three seasons (committee.SEMI_PAIRS_FROM, SEMI_PAIR_ROLL; bowl_rotation). 2043 Redwood-501, 2044 Lumber-Star, 2045 Copper-Steam, repeating. 2038-2042 stay on the old roll (2042 semis: Star-Steam). committee.semi_title_overlap(season) reports any semifinal city that is also that year's awarded title city. Backup: committee.py.pre_semi_pairs.

2042 post-season: title_site_check(season, city) added (rotation-bowl city allowed for title only in a year it hosts a QF; barred if semi site). Backup committee.py.pre_title_check.
